00:22:11.096 --> 00:22:13.198 align:start size:81% position:19%
George Washington,
it's folded up.

00:22:13.198 --> 00:22:15.167
George Washington then takes it

00:22:15.167 --> 00:22:18.837
and he puts it in his letter.

00:22:18.837 --> 00:22:22.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is a letter to
the governor who says,

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:23.508
hey, I want to tell
you about the war.

00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:25.711
Here's the Colonel's message.

00:22:25.711 --> 00:22:27.746
So he takes this message,
puts it in his letter.

00:22:27.746 --> 00:22:32.150
That's his signature,
no, it's one of these.

00:22:33.318 --> 00:22:35.587
I think this is the
Washington signature.

00:22:35.587 --> 00:22:37.956 align:start size:97% position:3%
No, that's George
Washington signature there.

00:22:37.956 --> 00:22:38.957
There he does it.

00:22:38.957 --> 00:22:40.425
He puts that letter in here.

00:22:40.425 --> 00:22:41.760
He sends it to the governor.

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:43.762
This is the governor's letter,

00:22:43.762 --> 00:22:45.997
where he takes both
of these letters,

00:22:45.997 --> 00:22:49.101 align:start size:88% position:13%
this is texting, this
is early American texts.

00:22:49.101 --> 00:22:50.602
- God, that these things exist.

00:22:54.206 --> 00:22:57.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you know who
Raoul Wallenberg is?

00:23:03.749 --> 00:23:08.420
- He got Jews out of Russia.

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:09.821
It's like yeah.

00:23:09.821 --> 00:23:14.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
- He was killed by the
Russians, he was in Budapest.

00:23:16.828 --> 00:23:20.832 align:start size:88% position:13%
I got this for Christmas
one year from my wife

00:23:20.832 --> 00:23:23.702
and she handed me a box
and she gave it to me

00:23:23.702 --> 00:23:26.772
and then she took it
back and she said,

00:23:26.772 --> 00:23:28.073
I can't give this to you.

00:23:28.073 --> 00:23:29.341
And I said, why?

00:23:29.341 --> 00:23:30.409
She said, I'll give
it to you tomorrow.

00:23:30.409 --> 00:23:31.877
I said what?

00:23:31.877 --> 00:23:34.780 align:start size:97% position:3%
She said, it's Christmas,
you will spend all day crying

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:36.248
if I give this to you.

00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:38.917 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm like, I'm not gonna
cry, she said, promise?

00:23:38.917 --> 00:23:40.919
'Cause I know you, you will.

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:43.155
And I said, I won't cry.

00:23:43.155 --> 00:23:46.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
She gave it to me, I spent
all Christmas crying.

00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:51.563
This is one of the most
powerful things I own.

00:23:53.632 --> 00:23:55.734
This is a Schutz-Pass.

00:23:55.734 --> 00:24:00.672 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a letter of protection
signed by Raoul Wallenberg.

00:24:03.275 --> 00:24:06.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
We asked him, okay, the
United States went to him.

00:24:06.945 --> 00:24:09.848
He's like, I don't know
what you would compare,

00:24:09.848 --> 00:24:11.383
the Nordstrom family.

00:24:11.383 --> 00:24:13.618
The Wallenberg family was
like the Nordstrom family

00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:15.687
on steroids.

00:24:15.687 --> 00:24:18.390 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they were very
powerful, very influential,

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:19.624
blah, blah blah.

00:24:19.624 --> 00:24:21.860
I think he was one
of the younger sons.

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:25.163
And the United States
went to him and said,

00:24:25.163 --> 00:24:30.168 align:start size:97% position:3%
listen, we think the Germans
are killing the Jews.

00:24:31.336 --> 00:24:33.538
We need somebody to
be our eyes and ears.

00:24:33.538 --> 00:24:37.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
Would you go over
with your government

00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:41.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
and work in your embassy
and tell us what's going on?

00:24:41.379 --> 00:24:46.384
He said, reluctantly, yes,
he knew what was at stake.

00:24:47.118 --> 00:24:48.620
He gets over there.

00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:51.923
He sees what's going on,
he not only reports back.

00:24:51.923 --> 00:24:54.759 align:start size:81% position:19%
He starts doing
this and his King,

00:24:54.759 --> 00:24:57.529 align:start size:81% position:19%
in letter after
letter, says stop,

00:24:57.529 --> 00:25:00.098
you know, we have
the Germans here.

00:25:00.098 --> 00:25:01.633
What are you doing?

00:25:01.633 --> 00:25:05.770
We are in trouble because you
are making all of these Jews,

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:07.672
citizens.

00:25:07.672 --> 00:25:10.842
This was a pass that said they
don't have to wear the star.

00:25:12.010 --> 00:25:15.881 align:start size:81% position:19%
This person now
belongs to Sweden.

00:25:17.082 --> 00:25:19.217 align:start size:88% position:13%
He would take these
and he would print them

00:25:19.217 --> 00:25:21.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
and sign them and
he'd go to the trains.

00:25:21.786 --> 00:25:24.389
And he'd stuff them
in between the cracks

00:25:24.389 --> 00:25:27.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the cattle cars, where
all the Jews were in.

00:25:27.859 --> 00:25:29.094
He'd stuffed them in

00:25:29.094 --> 00:25:32.297
and he'd stand on the
top of the last car.

00:25:32.297 --> 00:25:36.635
And he'd say, stop the train,
you have the wrong people.

00:25:36.635 --> 00:25:39.271
These people are my citizens.

00:25:39.271 --> 00:25:40.539
And they would unload.

00:25:40.539 --> 00:25:43.708
And everybody who
had one was free.

00:25:45.110 --> 00:25:50.115 align:start size:88% position:13%
The problem is he didn't
know when to stop.

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:55.420
And, the Russians were
coming in and he said,

00:25:59.157 --> 00:26:01.593
one of the people with the
Schutz-Pass said, Raoul,

00:26:01.593 --> 00:26:02.561
you've got to come with us.

00:26:02.561 --> 00:26:03.995
You've got to get out now.

00:26:03.995 --> 00:26:06.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, no, the
Russians are right there.

00:26:06.965 --> 00:26:10.468
They can't be as
bad as the Germans.

00:26:10.468 --> 00:26:13.438
There's too many people
that we'll leave behind.

00:26:13.438 --> 00:26:18.443
So he was last seen running
into the soldiers of Russia.

00:26:20.912 --> 00:26:23.114 align:start size:84% position:16%
We don't know whatever
happened to him.

00:26:23.114 --> 00:26:25.850 align:start size:88% position:13%
The United States of
America didn't even ask,

00:26:25.850 --> 00:26:29.321 align:start size:81% position:19%
didn't even ask
until Gerald Ford,

00:26:32.157 --> 00:26:34.259
there's a couple of
endings to the story.

00:26:34.259 --> 00:26:36.995
One that he died in a work camp

00:26:36.995 --> 00:26:40.999 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the late sixties,
early seventies,

00:26:40.999 --> 00:26:45.170
others was that he was shot
on the ground in Budapest,

00:26:45.170 --> 00:26:47.672
which we doubt because Stalin

00:26:47.672 --> 00:26:50.609 align:start size:88% position:13%
wanted to interrogate
him himself, personally.

00:26:51.810 --> 00:26:56.114 align:start size:88% position:13%
The most likely death
was that he was tortured

00:26:56.114 --> 00:27:01.052
and treated horribly and
died before 1955, I think.

00:27:03.054 --> 00:27:04.289 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I just wanna clarify
one thing though,

00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:06.458
you said that they were
my citizens of Sweden,

00:27:06.458 --> 00:27:09.060
but you meant Budapest, or am I-

00:27:09.060 --> 00:27:14.065
- He was making the Jews in
Budapest citizens of Sweden.

00:27:18.069 --> 00:27:21.539
So he was invoking the
protection of the King

00:27:21.539 --> 00:27:26.277 align:start size:97% position:3%
of Sweden, which caused
Sweden all kinds of trouble.

00:27:26.277 --> 00:27:27.812
- Okay, got it, got it,
I thought you were saying

00:27:27.812 --> 00:27:29.981
that he was somehow being
able to do this in Germany

00:27:29.981 --> 00:27:31.716
by saying that they
were citizens of-

00:27:31.716 --> 00:27:34.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No, no, no, no,
they were in Budapest,

00:27:34.119 --> 00:27:37.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they were being
claimed as Swedish citizens

00:27:37.822 --> 00:27:39.290
so they could travel.

00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:40.892
- I'm embarrassed that I
don't know more about this.

00:27:40.892 --> 00:27:43.428
- This guy, most people
don't know who he is.

00:27:43.428 --> 00:27:46.297
This is, I found this in auction

00:27:46.297 --> 00:27:51.302
and this is so nothing
on its own about this,

00:27:52.771 --> 00:27:57.676
it says, January, 2013, this
is a Russian cigarette case

00:27:59.978 --> 00:28:01.646
that happened to be carried,

00:28:01.646 --> 00:28:06.317
and it was all explained,
but no one tied it to this.

00:28:06.317 --> 00:28:09.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
And when I saw it for sale,
I was like, oh my gosh,

00:28:09.487 --> 00:28:12.857
this cigarette case was
carried by a man that was

00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:17.862
in the brigade that
went into Budapest,

00:28:18.596 --> 00:28:20.532
that he ran into.

00:28:20.532 --> 00:28:22.000
This cigarette case, on it,

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:26.371 align:start size:97% position:3%
it says in Russian, let's
kill all the Jews and go home.

00:28:28.239 --> 00:28:31.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
As he's saying, they
can't be as bad.

00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:33.812
This is who he's running to.

00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:37.649
One last piece that I brought.

00:28:38.917 --> 00:28:40.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I saw this one right
when we sat down,

00:28:40.819 --> 00:28:41.686
I said, who's is that?

00:28:41.686 --> 00:28:42.520
You said, wait.

00:28:52.363 --> 00:28:54.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
- John Huntsman,
John Huntsman Senior

00:28:54.666 --> 00:28:55.967
was a dear friend of mine.

00:28:56.901 --> 00:29:01.773
And he said, who
are your heroes?

00:29:03.675 --> 00:29:05.009
And I told him a few people.

00:29:05.009 --> 00:29:07.746 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he came to my
office a few weeks later

00:29:09.180 --> 00:29:13.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he sat down, he looked
at my desk and he said,

00:29:14.853 --> 00:29:16.855 align:start size:81% position:19%
I see the pictures
of your family.

00:29:16.855 --> 00:29:17.956
Where are your heroes?

00:29:18.957 --> 00:29:22.160
And I said, what do you mean?

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:27.165
He said, if you don't gaze
upon the faces of people

00:29:28.032 --> 00:29:30.101
that you want to be like,

00:29:31.302 --> 00:29:33.972
when you have a tough moment,

00:29:33.972 --> 00:29:38.576
you have to look down and
see somebody who stood.

00:29:40.078 --> 00:29:42.413 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's why I like Raoul
Wallenberg so much,

00:29:42.413 --> 00:29:44.415
this amazing, amazing man.

00:29:45.884 --> 00:29:50.889
This is a copy of "Mein
Kampf" all in lambskin,

00:29:52.390 --> 00:29:54.826
given by Hitler himself.

00:29:55.927 --> 00:29:57.495
And if you see the book plate.

00:30:04.435 --> 00:30:08.373 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Franz Schenk Freiherr
Von Stauffenberg.

00:30:08.373 --> 00:30:10.241
- You know who that is?

00:30:10.241 --> 00:30:14.312 align:start size:88% position:13%
Von Stauffenberg,
General Von Stauffenberg

00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:16.047
or what was he?

00:30:16.047 --> 00:30:17.549
I think he was a general,

00:30:17.549 --> 00:30:22.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
Von Stauffenberg, you
see the Tom cruise film?

00:30:24.222 --> 00:30:25.957
That's Von Stauffenberg.

00:30:27.458 --> 00:30:32.463 align:start position:0%
Von Stauffenberg fought against
the Nazis from the inside.

00:30:33.932 --> 00:30:37.702
He's the guy who went and
planned, placed the bomb.

00:30:38.870 --> 00:30:40.305
I actually don't have it here,

00:30:40.305 --> 00:30:43.775 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I have the napkin
from that bombing

00:30:43.775 --> 00:30:48.746
that was said to be the one
that Hitler had at that time.

00:30:50.114 --> 00:30:52.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's bloodstained,
shrapnel holes through it.

00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:57.322
This is his copy
of "Mein Kampf."

00:30:57.322 --> 00:31:00.725
When he said I'm not a Nazi,

00:31:01.826 --> 00:31:04.229 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know not only
because of what he did,

00:31:05.263 --> 00:31:07.599 line:0%
but the pages are perfect.

00:31:07.599 --> 00:31:09.901 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
These books had
never been opened.

00:31:12.804 --> 00:31:14.439
- God, it's eerie
just holding this.

00:31:14.439 --> 00:31:15.807
- It is, isn't it?

00:31:15.807 --> 00:31:19.010
And it's a weird thing
cause it's "Mein Kampf,"

00:31:19.010 --> 00:31:20.812
but it's Von Stauffenberg's.

00:31:24.182 --> 00:31:26.251 align:start size:84% position:16%
And don't judge people
by what they read

00:31:26.251 --> 00:31:29.287
or what they have or
what they might have.

00:31:29.287 --> 00:31:34.292
Don't judge people and he
and Dietrich Bonhoeffer,

00:31:38.029 --> 00:31:39.931
Raoul Wallenberg.

00:31:39.931 --> 00:31:44.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
These guys all acted
because nobody would act

00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:48.873
when they could.

00:31:50.108 --> 00:31:53.878
No one, the people,
I went to Auschwitz

00:31:53.878 --> 00:31:56.347
and I brought my
kids, this is 2012,

00:31:57.615 --> 00:32:00.551
and we were going to
Israel for vacation

00:32:00.551 --> 00:32:02.053
and I was bringing
the whole family.

00:32:02.053 --> 00:32:04.756
And I said, you can't go to
Israel for the first time

00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:08.927
unless you pass through the
gates of Auschwitz first.

00:32:08.927 --> 00:32:11.629
And my wife said, honey,

00:32:11.629 --> 00:32:14.465
that doesn't make it
really a vacation.

00:32:14.465 --> 00:32:15.833
And I said,

00:32:15.833 --> 00:32:19.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want the kids to understand
why Israel is there.

00:32:19.938 --> 00:32:23.341
And I want them to
make a choice now,

00:32:23.341 --> 00:32:27.412
when they're young, who
are you going to be?

00:32:27.412 --> 00:32:31.049 align:start size:88% position:13%
If the world goes
insane, who will you be?

00:32:32.216 --> 00:32:36.854 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I engaged a
woman, she was oh,

00:32:36.854 --> 00:32:40.258
in her eighties and so sweet.

00:32:40.258 --> 00:32:42.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
She was one of the
Righteous Among The Nations,

00:32:42.260 --> 00:32:45.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
which are the Christians
that saved Jews.

00:32:45.863 --> 00:32:49.133 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we went through Auschwitz
and then we met with her.

00:32:49.133 --> 00:32:52.470 align:start size:88% position:13%
And as we were leaving,
she told us this,

00:32:52.470 --> 00:32:54.372 align:start size:88% position:13%
she sat down with a
family for like an hour.

00:32:54.372 --> 00:32:57.308
It was just amazing.

00:32:57.308 --> 00:33:00.645
And she told us how
at 16 years old,

00:33:00.645 --> 00:33:04.248
she saw a Jew on the
street, just starving.

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:05.483
You could only feed a Jew,

00:33:05.483 --> 00:33:08.753 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think 400 or 800
calories a day.

00:33:08.753 --> 00:33:11.823
And just starving, and
it was a girl her age.

00:33:11.823 --> 00:33:14.292
And she said, please,
do you have any food?

00:33:14.292 --> 00:33:15.760
She said, I don't.

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:18.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you come here tomorrow,
I'll bring you something.

00:33:18.796 --> 00:33:22.200
So she came, she sat down at
the dinner table that night

00:33:22.200 --> 00:33:24.502
with her mom and dad and
they were eating dinner.

00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:27.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this a death
sentence, you feed a Jew,

00:33:27.005 --> 00:33:29.674
you get the same thing
as a death sentence.

00:33:29.674 --> 00:33:32.410
And she said, mama, dad, I
have to tell you something.

00:33:32.410 --> 00:33:36.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
She said, I promised I would
bring some food tomorrow

00:33:36.814 --> 00:33:40.318
to this Jewish girl
who was starving.

00:33:40.318 --> 00:33:43.755 align:start size:97% position:3%
And she said, she remembers
the whole room, just stopping.

00:33:43.755 --> 00:33:46.724 align:start size:88% position:13%
And her mom and dad
putting their spoon down

00:33:46.724 --> 00:33:48.726
and looking at each other
and staring at each other,

00:33:48.726 --> 00:33:50.595
not saying anything.

00:33:50.595 --> 00:33:52.096
And then her mom got up,

00:33:52.096 --> 00:33:57.035
she started pulling a big pot
out and put it on the stove.

00:33:58.202 --> 00:33:59.704 align:start size:84% position:16%
And Paulina said, what
are you doing mom?

00:33:59.704 --> 00:34:03.408 align:start size:84% position:16%
She said, well, if
she's coming for food,

00:34:03.408 --> 00:34:06.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
she'll clearly have
hungry friends.

00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:09.981
They saved about a hundred Jews.

00:34:09.981 --> 00:34:13.785
So after I talked to her,
I said to her, Paulina,

00:34:13.785 --> 00:34:17.455
what do you, how do I water
the seed of righteousness

00:34:17.455 --> 00:34:19.390
in myself and in my family?

00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:20.825
What do you do to
strengthen that?

00:34:20.825 --> 00:34:22.193
That seed is there.

00:34:22.193 --> 00:34:25.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
How do we make it into
a tree so we stand?

00:34:25.129 --> 00:34:26.831
And she looked at me
and said something

00:34:26.831 --> 00:34:28.699
that I thought was profound.

00:34:28.699 --> 00:34:33.438
But up until recently, I
didn't truly understand.

00:34:33.438 --> 00:34:36.908
And she said, you misunderstand,

00:34:38.276 --> 00:34:40.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
the righteous didn't
suddenly become righteous.

00:34:40.511 --> 00:34:42.814 align:start size:84% position:16%
They just refused
to go over the cliff

00:34:42.814 --> 00:34:44.515
with the rest of humanity.

00:34:44.515 --> 00:34:46.984
That's fantastic.

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:49.687
We don't have to do, you
don't ever have to get to

00:34:49.687 --> 00:34:50.822
Von Stauffenberg,

00:34:52.023 --> 00:34:54.992
all you have to do is
say, no that's crazy,

00:34:54.992 --> 00:34:57.628
I know what I saw, that's
a car burning behind you,

00:34:57.628 --> 00:35:02.400
that's Antifa, that's a riot,
that's looting, that's wrong.

00:35:02.400 --> 00:35:03.501
- [Dave] Mostly peaceful.

00:35:03.501 --> 00:35:05.470
- Yeah, it's not
mostly peaceful.

00:35:05.470 --> 00:35:09.540 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm sorry, you're going over
the cliff into insanity.

00:35:09.540 --> 00:35:12.844
I'm standing where
I've always stood.

00:35:12.844 --> 00:35:15.046 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You know, it's interesting,
I often think now,

00:35:15.046 --> 00:35:17.148
now that I've been taking
some of these positions

00:35:17.148 --> 00:35:19.083 align:start size:84% position:16%
that aren't thought
of as popular

00:35:19.083 --> 00:35:22.086 align:start size:88% position:13%
or okayed by
mainstream or whatever,

00:35:22.086 --> 00:35:23.988
that the only thing to
fear is fear itself.

00:35:23.988 --> 00:35:25.756
And I've been thinking
about that a lot lately

00:35:25.756 --> 00:35:27.925
that the more that I say,

00:35:27.925 --> 00:35:29.360
the things that I
believe to be true,

00:35:29.360 --> 00:35:31.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
that happened to be against
the mainstream things.

00:35:31.863 --> 00:35:33.498
The more I get over that,

00:35:33.498 --> 00:35:34.899
because if you can
get over the fear,

00:35:34.899 --> 00:35:37.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
then if it's true
that we're on a list

00:35:37.268 --> 00:35:40.638
and they're coming for
us, then we're on a list,

00:35:40.638 --> 00:35:42.907 align:start size:97% position:3%
and by the way, pretty much
everyone's on the list.

00:35:42.907 --> 00:35:45.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's why there's
that famous thing.

00:35:45.042 --> 00:35:46.410
You know, they came
for the Jews first.

00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:49.013
It's like, we're all
part of this thing,

00:35:49.013 --> 00:35:50.414
but it's a very strange time

00:35:50.414 --> 00:35:53.117
that you can show me
some of these things,

00:35:53.117 --> 00:35:55.853 align:start size:88% position:13%
founding documents
from the United States,

00:35:55.853 --> 00:35:59.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
documents about saving
Jews during World War Two.

00:35:59.323 --> 00:36:03.027 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it feels like something
that's kind of now.

00:36:03.027 --> 00:36:06.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Only if people don't
find their courage.

00:36:06.898 --> 00:36:11.102 align:start position:0%
I truly believe and this is
why I think you're so powerful,

00:36:12.770 --> 00:36:17.775 align:start size:97% position:3%
courage is contagious, it
is, not everybody's a leader,

00:36:18.976 --> 00:36:21.612
not everybody's willing
to step out into danger,

00:36:23.314 --> 00:36:24.782
not everybody's willing to lose

00:36:24.782 --> 00:36:27.685
all their friends
or to whatever,

00:36:27.685 --> 00:36:31.856 align:start size:88% position:13%
but when they see
someone risk everything

00:36:31.856 --> 00:36:35.560
and they see them on a list,

00:36:35.560 --> 00:36:39.463
if you can get them early
enough, they'll step out.

00:36:39.463 --> 00:36:43.034 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the longer you
wait, the worse it gets,

00:36:43.034 --> 00:36:46.737 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's Bonhoeffer,
was a pacifist,

00:36:46.737 --> 00:36:51.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
was involved in Von
Stauffenberg's coup, how?

00:36:52.443 --> 00:36:54.245
He's a pacifist.

00:36:54.245 --> 00:36:59.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
He said, there's nothing
else we can do at this point

00:36:59.016 --> 00:37:00.785
because it's too late.

00:37:00.785 --> 00:37:03.554
The people's hearts
had turned to stone

00:37:03.554 --> 00:37:05.323
and you couldn't turn them.

00:37:05.323 --> 00:37:08.526
We have to find a way to
make sure that our hearts

00:37:08.526 --> 00:37:11.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the hearts of everybody
we know, stay soft,

00:37:11.596 --> 00:37:14.665 align:start size:84% position:16%
and see people as
people, not enemies.

00:37:14.665 --> 00:37:16.234
- You know, when I was
on tour with Jordan,

00:37:16.234 --> 00:37:17.902
one of the things that
he would bring up often,

00:37:17.902 --> 00:37:20.671 align:start size:97% position:3%
because he would talk about
the parallels to Nazism

00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.873 align:start size:97% position:3%
to some of the authoritarian
movements of the day.

00:37:22.873 --> 00:37:24.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he would say to
everyone in the crowd,

00:37:24.375 --> 00:37:25.776
he'd say you know,

00:37:25.776 --> 00:37:28.346 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's 3000 of you
sitting out here right now.

00:37:28.346 --> 00:37:32.083
And I guarantee you that every
single one of you would think

00:37:32.083 --> 00:37:36.254
that you wouldn't be a Nazi
if this was 1936 Germany.

00:37:36.254 --> 00:37:40.291 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that proves probably
that you would be.

00:37:40.291 --> 00:37:42.126
And I always thought that
that was pretty powerful.

00:37:42.126 --> 00:37:44.762
We all think we would
do the unpopular thing.

00:37:44.762 --> 00:37:46.897
We all think we would
do the risky thing.

00:37:46.897 --> 00:37:49.834
We all judge everybody by
our standards of today.

00:37:49.834 --> 00:37:51.869
- I'm not sure I'd
stand in the end.

00:37:53.104 --> 00:37:57.341
I mean, a friend of
mine, Marcus Trell,

00:37:58.776 --> 00:38:03.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
I said to him, how do you
stand torture and not break?

00:38:04.949 --> 00:38:08.586 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said, Glenn, everyone
breaks, everyone breaks.

00:38:08.586 --> 00:38:12.857
He said, but the ones
who break the fastest

00:38:12.857 --> 00:38:15.159 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the loudest are
the ones who will say,

00:38:16.027 --> 00:38:18.362
I'll stand, oh, I'll stand,

00:38:18.362 --> 00:38:21.065 align:start size:84% position:16%
because they haven't
thought about it.

00:38:21.065 --> 00:38:22.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's why I wanted to bring
my kids to Auschwitz.

00:38:22.867 --> 00:38:25.002
I need you to feel it.

00:38:25.002 --> 00:38:27.071
So you can think about it

00:38:27.071 --> 00:38:30.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
and really look at
this as a possibility.

00:38:30.107 --> 00:38:35.112
And once you do that and you
realize by the grace of God

00:38:35.980 --> 00:38:40.117
I'll stand, then you're ready.

00:38:41.585 --> 00:38:45.289
But we have got to prepare
ourselves now to be ready

00:38:46.724 --> 00:38:50.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
because if you're ready
now, the problems go away.

00:38:50.294 --> 00:38:52.396
They think you're sheep.

00:38:52.396 --> 00:38:56.100 align:start position:0%
I mean, I asked you on a
podcast with you the last time.

00:38:56.100 --> 00:38:58.135
Where's the line?

00:38:58.135 --> 00:39:00.137
What line do you have

00:39:00.137 --> 00:39:03.941
as an individual that
you say I won't cross?

00:39:04.875 --> 00:39:06.243
Well, I won't go there.

00:39:06.243 --> 00:39:09.146
I mean, if I said to
you last summer, yeah,

00:39:09.146 --> 00:39:10.481
they're going to tell us

00:39:10.481 --> 00:39:13.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we can't have
Thanksgiving with our family,

00:39:13.217 --> 00:39:15.252
that we have to wear
a mask all the time.

00:39:15.252 --> 00:39:17.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the president is
going to make that mandate

00:39:17.355 --> 00:39:19.457
and they're going to
shut down the economy.

00:39:19.457 --> 00:39:23.894
You and I, and everybody else
would have said never, never.

00:39:23.894 --> 00:39:25.162
- I would have said you know,

00:39:25.162 --> 00:39:27.198
maybe they're right
about that bad guy.

00:39:27.198 --> 00:39:30.868 align:start position:0%
- Right, you would've, you
would've, it's insane to think,

00:39:30.868 --> 00:39:32.903
look where we are.

00:39:32.903 --> 00:39:35.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
And now all of a
sudden that's normal.

00:39:36.841 --> 00:39:38.776
It's the new normal.

00:39:38.776 --> 00:39:41.479
- Yeah, they get you with
that phrase the new normal,

00:39:41.479 --> 00:39:42.880
because there's an implicit,

00:39:42.880 --> 00:39:46.317
oh, accept it, it
it's implicitly,

00:39:46.317 --> 00:39:48.085
it's here, so you
better accept it.

00:39:48.085 --> 00:39:50.187
- So the thing about war is

00:39:51.455 --> 00:39:54.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
war is just about
changing leadership,

00:39:54.592 --> 00:39:56.994
borders and financial systems.

00:39:56.994 --> 00:39:59.063
That's what war is really about

00:39:59.063 --> 00:40:01.031
for the people up at the top.

00:40:01.031 --> 00:40:03.868
And it's usually so horrible

00:40:03.868 --> 00:40:08.105 align:start size:88% position:13%
that a society even,
great ones never go back

00:40:08.105 --> 00:40:09.707
to the way they were

00:40:09.707 --> 00:40:14.478 align:start size:88% position:13%
because you're so
willing to accept peace.

00:40:14.478 --> 00:40:17.281
I just want to go back to normal

00:40:17.281 --> 00:40:19.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you never
reset back to normal

00:40:19.683 --> 00:40:21.786
and you'll accept
almost anything.

00:40:21.786 --> 00:40:23.254
Here we are.

00:40:24.688 --> 00:40:27.024
Look at what we're willing
to accept at this point.

00:40:27.024 --> 00:40:28.726
And I know I did when
they started talking

00:40:28.726 --> 00:40:29.660
about the new normal

00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:31.128
I was like, no, no, no, no, no,

00:40:31.128 --> 00:40:34.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want a new normal,
I want normal, normal

00:40:34.365 --> 00:40:36.000 align:start size:81% position:19%
- [Dave] Normal
will be just fine.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:39.403
- How many people now would
just be happy if we just,

00:40:39.403 --> 00:40:41.572 align:start size:84% position:16%
if we had, okay,
this is a new normal,

00:40:41.572 --> 00:40:44.742
and they're gonna start you
know, letting things back up,

00:40:44.742 --> 00:40:46.644
but it's never going
to get the way it was,

00:40:46.644 --> 00:40:48.145
lots, lots would accept that.

00:40:48.145 --> 00:40:50.314
- Is that why you care
so much about history

00:40:50.314 --> 00:40:51.615
and these things,

00:40:51.615 --> 00:40:53.384
because you feel like
it kind of grounds you

00:40:53.384 --> 00:40:55.219 align:start size:88% position:13%
to do the current events
that you gotta do.

00:40:55.219 --> 00:40:56.787
You gotta wake up every day.

00:40:56.787 --> 00:40:59.990
You do how many hours a day
of talk, at least, at least?

00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:02.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Five, give or take.
- That's a lot of airtime.

00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:05.696
I know how much I talk and
it ain't five hours a day

00:41:05.696 --> 00:41:08.065
but is that why you care
so much about history?

00:41:08.065 --> 00:41:10.901 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because otherwise you're
just sort of spinning

00:41:10.901 --> 00:41:13.437
in the morass of the day.

00:41:13.437 --> 00:41:15.573 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I know clearly what
I'm fighting for,

00:41:15.573 --> 00:41:17.608
I know clearly what
I'm fighting against

00:41:18.542 --> 00:41:22.580 line:0%
and my son was eight maybe.

00:41:22.580 --> 00:41:24.715 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
And he started
taking Tae Kwon Do

00:41:24.715 --> 00:41:27.284 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and he had to go in
to get his first belt.

00:41:27.284 --> 00:41:28.786
And I don't know why,

00:41:28.786 --> 00:41:32.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he didn't expect
there to be a crowd there.

00:41:32.256 --> 00:41:35.426
And when he was really
young crowds scared him

00:41:35.426 --> 00:41:40.431 align:start size:88% position:13%
because of the stuff
that has happened to me,

00:41:41.799 --> 00:41:44.201 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he witnessed as a little
kid, crowds scared him.

00:41:44.201 --> 00:41:46.837
And he didn't want
to be around crowds

00:41:46.837 --> 00:41:49.306
and he didn't want to
be noticed, you know?

00:41:50.541 --> 00:41:52.610
And so we're going and
he's like, no, no, no,

00:41:52.610 --> 00:41:54.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
there's a crowd,
no, there's a crowd.

00:41:54.411 --> 00:41:56.981 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm like, Ray, it's
going to be fine, it's fine,

00:41:56.981 --> 00:41:58.549
it's okay, just the parents.

00:41:58.549 --> 00:42:00.918
They're just like us, we're
just watching your friends.

00:42:00.918 --> 00:42:04.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
No, no, no, no, and
he really freaked out.

00:42:04.288 --> 00:42:05.789
So I had to take him home

00:42:05.789 --> 00:42:08.659
while his sister got her
belt and I'm driving home,

00:42:08.659 --> 00:42:11.028
and I'm like, what
do I say to him?

00:42:12.062 --> 00:42:14.098
And I, quite frankly,

00:42:14.098 --> 00:42:15.332
it was a little pissed

00:42:15.332 --> 00:42:16.767 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I didn't want
to be pissed at him,

00:42:16.767 --> 00:42:19.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause he wasn't, you know,
he wasn't misbehaving.

00:42:19.670 --> 00:42:24.675 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we drove home and I
held his hand the whole time

00:42:25.543 --> 00:42:26.710
but we didn't really talk.

00:42:26.710 --> 00:42:27.912 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause I'm thinking
what do I say,

00:42:29.079 --> 00:42:31.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
pulled into the house,
got into the house.

00:42:31.181 --> 00:42:33.717
And I knew exactly
what I needed to do.

00:42:33.717 --> 00:42:36.253
And I said come into
my library, come on,

00:42:36.253 --> 00:42:38.122
sit down in the library.

00:42:38.122 --> 00:42:42.192 align:start position:0%
And at that time, my whole walls
were covered with artifacts

00:42:42.192 --> 00:42:45.663
and men determined to be
free and Raoul Wallenberg

00:42:45.663 --> 00:42:47.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the picture of the
woman that he saved

00:42:47.798 --> 00:42:51.669
and a picture of him, all
of the heroes, Rosa Parks,

00:42:51.669 --> 00:42:53.771
everybody, Winston Churchill.

00:42:54.738 --> 00:42:56.040
And we sat there on the couch.

00:42:56.040 --> 00:42:58.008
I said, just want you
to look at the walls.

00:42:59.276 --> 00:43:00.744
And he did.

00:43:00.744 --> 00:43:03.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, why do you
think I have them up here?

00:43:03.814 --> 00:43:06.584
And he said because
they're all heroes

00:43:06.584 --> 00:43:08.886
and they weren't afraid,
and they do the thing.

00:43:08.886 --> 00:43:10.621
And I said, no,

00:43:11.789 --> 00:43:13.791
because I know each
and every one of them

00:43:13.791 --> 00:43:18.796
was terrified of doing what
they knew they had to do.

00:43:19.930 --> 00:43:22.533 align:start size:84% position:16%
They were terrified,
but they did it.

00:43:23.801 --> 00:43:28.072
That's the lesson of history.

00:43:28.072 --> 00:43:29.273
They're just like you,

00:43:29.273 --> 00:43:31.775 align:start size:88% position:13%
Abraham Lincoln was
not a big, tall statue.

00:43:31.775 --> 00:43:34.244
He knew he was going to die.

00:43:34.244 --> 00:43:39.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
He knew it, he did it
anyway, he didn't want to,

00:43:39.016 --> 00:43:40.751
nobody wants to.

00:43:40.751 --> 00:43:42.286
Do you think Gandhi?

00:43:42.286 --> 00:43:45.122
Well Gandhi may have, because
he was doing the hunger strike

00:43:45.122 --> 00:43:48.792
but that was against his own
people, his own followers,

00:43:48.792 --> 00:43:53.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was like you want to
be full of anger and rage,

00:43:53.330 --> 00:43:54.565
I'm not with you.

00:43:54.565 --> 00:43:58.002
And until my followers
stop acting that way

00:43:58.002 --> 00:43:59.903
I'll starve myself to death.

00:43:59.903 --> 00:44:02.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, these
people were amazing,

00:44:02.439 --> 00:44:06.510
but all of them had
a change of heart

00:44:06.510 --> 00:44:07.778
and didn't want to do it.

00:44:09.213 --> 00:44:13.984
Bonhoeffer, he was here in
America, he escaped Germany.

00:44:15.152 --> 00:44:17.254
And he went back to, he
came here to America,

00:44:17.254 --> 00:44:19.390
he was in New York and
he was so guilt-ridden

00:44:19.390 --> 00:44:24.395
that he left his people in this
dark hour that he went back.

00:44:25.529 --> 00:44:26.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it was on
one of the last boats

00:44:26.964 --> 00:44:29.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
that went back and you
could get back into Germany.

00:44:29.767 --> 00:44:34.138
He went back and he said
to all of his pupils okay,

00:44:34.138 --> 00:44:36.740
let's say you're an atheist,
let's say you're an atheist,

00:44:36.740 --> 00:44:38.609
you really believe that,

00:44:38.609 --> 00:44:41.111
but you don't have
any other choice

00:44:41.111 --> 00:44:43.147
than to take somebody's life.

00:44:43.147 --> 00:44:45.549
They didn't realize at
the time the example

00:44:45.549 --> 00:44:49.486
he was trying to get
them to convince him

00:44:49.486 --> 00:44:51.221
that there's no way
you could do that.

00:44:51.221 --> 00:44:53.657
Or to accept, convince him that,

00:44:53.657 --> 00:44:58.328 align:start position:0%
yes, I can do that, he's
involved with Von Stauffenberg,

00:44:58.328 --> 00:45:01.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
he's taken to a concentration
camp in the end.

00:45:01.865 --> 00:45:05.102
He's in a cell with a
guy who took the Jews

00:45:05.102 --> 00:45:08.806 align:start size:88% position:13%
up into airplanes until
their heads popped.

00:45:08.806 --> 00:45:12.242
He took people and
covered them in ice

00:45:12.242 --> 00:45:15.446 align:start size:97% position:3%
and freezing in the cold
water and all of that stuff,

00:45:15.446 --> 00:45:19.550 align:start position:0%
in every hospital in the world,
that book from the Nazis,

00:45:19.550 --> 00:45:23.454 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of those stats are in
every hospital in the world.

00:45:23.454 --> 00:45:26.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's why he was sent
to a concentration camp

00:45:26.790 --> 00:45:28.392
because Hitler,

00:45:28.392 --> 00:45:31.161 align:start size:97% position:3%
he released all this
information and Hitler said,

00:45:31.161 --> 00:45:32.896
what the hell are you doing?

00:45:32.896 --> 00:45:34.531
And he said, you know how
many lives will be saved

00:45:34.531 --> 00:45:35.699
by this information?

00:45:35.699 --> 00:45:37.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
He said, we're
saving German lives,

00:45:37.601 --> 00:45:39.303
not everybody's life.

00:45:39.303 --> 00:45:44.308 align:start size:97% position:3%
He, a prostitute, double
agent, and Dietrich Bonhoeffer

00:45:45.075 --> 00:45:46.844
were in the same cell.

00:45:46.844 --> 00:45:50.514
They were all executed four
days before Hitler died.

00:45:50.514 --> 00:45:54.017
The guy at the gallows
remembers Bonhoeffer

00:45:54.017 --> 00:45:55.619
because he thanked him.

00:45:56.687 --> 00:45:58.789 align:start size:88% position:13%
He walked up the
stairs and he got there

00:45:58.789 --> 00:46:02.192
and the executioner
kind of helped him up

00:46:02.192 --> 00:46:04.394 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then put the
noose around his neck.

00:46:04.394 --> 00:46:06.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
And Bonhoeffer looked
at him and said,

00:46:06.764 --> 00:46:08.332
thank you for your kindness.

00:46:09.299 --> 00:46:10.400
Good gallows.

00:46:11.769 --> 00:46:13.604
That's the person I want to be,

00:46:13.604 --> 00:46:15.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
but that's not a
person you just become,

00:46:15.973 --> 00:46:18.876
that's a person you
work hard to become.

00:46:20.711 --> 00:46:22.045
- Glenn, I didn't know
what we were going to do

00:46:22.045 --> 00:46:23.213
when we sat down.

00:46:23.213 --> 00:46:24.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said to you, right,
as we walked in,

00:46:24.414 --> 00:46:26.116 align:start size:81% position:19%
I said, let's just
figure it out.

